::: callout-note
## *tl;dr:* Probably 13.
:::

Sounds like a simple problem, but it isn't.

It's pretty common for sports teams to set a goal at the start of a season to make the finals/playoffs . Teams in the NRL[^1] are no different. The flaw in this goal is that it's a moving target; the number of wins needed to qualify varies from season-to-season depending on the results of other teams. A 12-win season (from 24 games) is enough to qualify some years, but not enough in others.

[^1]: National Rugby League

So how many wins do teams need to be confident they'll qualify?

